{"success":true,"data":{"tools":[{"provider":"github-com","capability":"repositories/advisory","description":"One GitHub Advisory Database record by GHSA id, CVE id or github.com/advisories URL: type (reviewed, unreviewed or malware), severity, CVSS v3 and v4, the EPSS exploit probability and percentile, CWE ids with names, every affected package with its vulnerable range, first patched version and vulnerable functions, credits (finder, reporter, remediation developer ...), references, the markdown description, and the GitHub review, NVD publication and withdrawal dates. Adds over osv-dev vuln and nvd-nist-gov cve: EPSS, CWE names, credit roles, the advisory type and vulnerable functions in one record. A CVE shared by several GHSA records returns the reviewed one and lists the rest. An unknown id is not_found. CC BY 4.0, attribute GitHub."},{"provider":"github-com","capability":"repositories/contributors","description":"One page of a repository's contributors ordered by commit count on the default branch, with login, account type and contribution count. Anonymous (email-only) contributors are not listed. GitHub refuses this listing for repositories with very large histories (for example torvalds/linux), which surfaces as an error naming the reason."},{"provider":"github-com","capability":"repositories/file","description":"The text of one file in a public GitHub repository at a branch, tag or commit, given as a raw.githubusercontent.com URL, a github.com blob URL, or repo plus path (ref defaults to HEAD, the default branch). One ranged GET to raw.githubusercontent.com, which does not use the REST API's 60/hour quota. Returns at most the first 1 MiB: size_bytes is the full size and truncated marks a cut file, reported as partial. A binary or non-UTF-8 file fails with invalid_input (not_text); a missing file, ref or repository is not_found."},{"provider":"github-com","capability":"repositories/issue_counts","description":"Exact issue counts for a repository (pull requests excluded, unlike the repository's open_issues_count): the total for the given state plus one count per requested label, from GitHub's issue search. Makes 1 + labels.length search requests; at most 5 labels per call because GitHub allows 10 keyless searches per minute per IP."},{"provider":"github-com","capability":"repositories/issues","description":"One page of a repository's issues filtered by state and labels (all given labels must match), sorted by created/updated/comments. Pull requests are excluded unless include_pull_requests is true, so a page may hold fewer than per_page records; pull_requests_excluded says how many were dropped. Each record carries title, state, labels, assignees, milestone, comment and reaction counts, body and timestamps."}],"web":[{"url":"https://www.kaggle.com/tobycrabtree/nfl-scores-and-betting-data/home","title":"NFL scores and betting data - Kaggle","description":"National Football League (NFL) game results since 1966 with betting odds information since 1979. Dataset was created from a variety of sources including games ...","position":1},{"url":"https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/tobycrabtree/nfl-scores-and-betting-data","title":"NFL scores and betting data | Kaggle","description":"# NFL scores and betting data\n## About Dataset\n### Context\nNational Football League historic game and betting info\n\n[[www.spreadspoke.com](http://www.spreadspoke.com)](http://www.spreadspoke.com/)\n\n### Content\nNational Football League (NFL) game results since 1966 with betting odds information since 1979. Betting data was used from [[http://www.repole.com/sun4cast/data.html](http://www.repole.com/sun4cast/data.html)](http://www.repole.com/sun4cast/data.html) for 1978-2013 seasons.\n\n### Acknowledgements\n[[https://github.com/fivethirtyeight/nfl-elo-game](https://github.com/fivethirtyeight/nfl-elo-game)](https://github.com/fivethirtyeight/nfl-elo-game)\n\n[[http://www.repole.com/sun4cast/data.html](http://www.repole.com/sun4cast/data.html)](http://www.repole.com/sun4cast/data.html)\n\n[[https://www.pro-football-reference.com/](https://www.pro-football-reference.com/)](https://www.pro-football-reference.com/)\n\n[[http://www.espn.com/nfl/](http://www.espn.com/nfl/)](http://www.espn.com/nfl/)\n\n[[http://www.nflweather.com/](http://www.nflweather.com/)](http://www.nflweather.com/)\n\n[[http://www.aussportsbetting.com/data/historical-nfl-results-and-odds-data/](http://www.aussportsbetting.com/data/historical-nfl-results-and-odds-data/)](http://www.aussportsbetting.com/data/historical-nfl-results-and-odds-data/)\n\n[[https://github.com/Nolanole/NFL-Weather-Project](https://github.com/Nolanole/NFL-Weather-Project)](https://github.com/Nolanole/NFL-Weather-Project)\n\n## Usability\ninfo\n\n10.00\n\n## Data Explorer\nVersion 82 (1.64 MB)\n\nspreadspoke.R\n\n## Metadata\n### DOI Citation\nkeyboard_arrow_down\n\n## Related Notebooks\nSee all\n\narrow_drop_up147\n\n[![](https://www.kaggleusercontent.com/kf/31917369/eyJhbGciOiJkaXIiLCJlbmMiOiJBMTI4Q0JDLUhTMjU2In0..2p8X-Rea4eJMNYNM_7vo4w.PvUjRjWI89Gbk9RaR_2Wr9AwX-tQz4E53Rb5bzkIdt-AZiNX6zk8XOscnqhQGx4v3Eb6AE-amZMhsIvcTDj9w642HaakQvEb2_xSiVZxjKh7kRTeyzHNXbmT2IuOTegkqp98-kgGKf5Es3y1IJckfebtX2iD0exdJCpOsYlPzkc9_awHFRcWWkP0tQUXbOrFrmjTyReIRRU0Tb9PE948LfLe9cBG1VfXACHdTy2ftATyoNh2jADnMLdC3DyTVKG4RvMQyOubLvDEFX_AxZOV1PN4yCH3XvBnDQvArH1eLAfbmuCks-GORh4ZYp3qhJh8RNBDdKDtZ_L2b0H2XHETIj103bmVmf2maTF32_QO_LmR2GmnfszzZL0JvI8Cl2_tw1qocHEGq8CVC9gzeYWFWwzal-rmfUcgJVj5GJQsmxsOSlia7KVwtqWuV9pjAxxfKMlk1xC6AZRqg5zix33nBm9WhJsQL0CTun36jVFA20XDaAXU9uqAFN0uKv14PBI5d4b6GpjOcGFyUFG11acZXEmehvySHX_EdRtk31Vp5o07-ek5YxRR2lk8QFFLIZGB2z7gk0ECrXiZLKDQkpfcedhe2uBrzgPLySStC8P2sTRDf3wuZY-b5TMH-0tKPqKhWWjRjMHHbfyR6Ew-pKDUGQ.IW_fOZAbE24JK3nOCJfwSQ/__results___files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-11-1.png)\\\n\\\nApplying Pythagorean Expectation to Major Sports\\\n\\\nmore_vert\\\n\\\nUpdated 7 years ago\\\n\\\nNHL Game Data+5](https://www.kaggle.com/code/jaseziv83/applying-pythagorean-expectation-to-major-sports)\n\narrow_drop_up115\n\n![](https://www.kaggle.com/static/images/medals/competitions/silverl@2x.png)[JasonZivkovic's profile (opens in a new tab)](https://www.kaggle.com/jaseziv83)\n\n[![](https://www.kaggle.com/static/images/dataset-deletion-icon@2x.png)\\\n\\\nSports Bets Winning Algorithm\\\n\\\nmore_vert\\\n\\\nUpdated 2 years ago\\\n[Private Datasource]+1](https://www.kaggle.com/code/dascient/sports-bets-winning-algorithm)\n\narrow_drop_up93\n\ntable_chart","position":2},{"url":"https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/tobycrabtree/nfl-scores-and-betting-data/code","title":"NFL scores and betting data - Kaggle","description":"Scores and descriptive game info for National Football League games.","position":3},{"url":"https://github.com/koltbern15/Sports-Betting","title":"koltbern15/Sports-Betting - GitHub","description":"# NFL Betting Analytics\nGamble responsibly.\n\nLoads historical NFL games + closing lines from a Kaggle CSV into SQLite and produces three per-bucket historical-edge reports (against-the-spread, totals over/under, and derived moneyline) with full statistical rigor (n, win rate, ROI at -110/-105, p-value vs the 52.38% breakeven, Wilson 95% CI, and by-season trend). Slice 3 validates the derived-ML report against real historical sportsbook moneylines from nflverse (2020–2024). Slice 6 ingests historical opening lines (two cross-validated sources); Slice 7 builds the CLV engine and finds the project's one real signal — the closing line is sharper than the open; Slice 8 adds a live \"This Week\" odds board (best price / line shopping + line movement + historical context).\n\nSlice 1 (ATS): `2026-05-26-nfl-betting-slice1-design.md` + `2026-05-26-nfl-betting-slice1.md`. Slice 2 (totals + moneyline): `2026-05-27-nfl-betting-slice2-design.md` + `2026-05-27-nfl-betting-slice2.md`. Slice 3 (real-line validation): `2026-05-27-nfl-betting-slice3-design.md` + `2026-05-27-nfl-betting-slice3.md`. Slice 4 (credible edges): `2026-05-27-nfl-betting-slice4-design.md` + `2026-05-27-nfl-betting-slice4.md`. Slice 5 (honest edge report): `2026-05-29-nfl-betting-slice5-design.md` + `2026-05-29-nfl-betting-slice5.md`.\n\n## Slice 5 — Honest edge report\n```\n# (one-time) verify Kaggle ATS/totals lines match nflverse on the 2020-2024 overlap\nuv run python scripts/cross_check_ats_totals.py\n\n# refresh per-market reports\nuv run python -m engine.ats\nuv run python -m engine.totals\nuv run python -m engine.validation\n\n# build the cross-market edge report\nuv run python -m engine.edge_report\n```\n\n## Slice 8 — Live This Week odds board\n[Permalink: Slice 8 — Live This Week odds board](https://github.com/koltbern15/Sports-Betting#slice-8--live-this-week-odds-board)\n\nHistorical stats from Slices 1–7 are surfaced as context — they are labeled, honest, and explicitly not certified picks.\n\n### What it does\n- **Historical context** — the CLV and ATS/totals bucket findings from earlier slices are shown alongside current lines as context. They are clearly labeled as historical analysis, not certified edges.\n\n## Slice 9 — Historical showcase tabs\n[Permalink: Slice 9 — Historical showcase tabs](https://github.com/koltbern15/Sports-Betting#slice-9--historical-showcase-tabs)\n\n**This Week** leads (the live odds board from Slice 8); the five showcase tabs surface the historical analysis built in Slices 1–7.\n\n- **Leans** — per game, an honest spread + total read: the historically-favored side _only_ when its bucket cleared the -110 breakeven (52.4%) with n≥50, else \"no lean\", always paired with the best available price across books. Recomputes from the sidebar season range (narrowing it → more \"no lean\"). Historical context + best price, never a prediction. No moneyline.\n\n## Scope\n- **Slice 8 (complete):** live This Week odds board — current odds + best price (line shopping) + line movement + historical context, refined-dark Streamlit, honest framing. Historical showcase tabs = Slice 9.","position":4,"category":"github"},{"url":"ht